  "description": "The WHEN OTHER arm of 9100-GETCARD-BYACCTCARD at :762-771 - an unexpected RESP from the CARDDAT read, which the seeded data alone cannot produce, so the outcome is forced. WS-FILE-ERROR-MESSAGE is composed at :767-770 from ERROR-OPNAME 'READ', ERROR-FILE 'CARDDAT ' in a PIC X(9) receiver, and the RESP and RESP2 values each rendered as nine unsigned digits left-justified in a PIC X(10) item; the 80-byte group is then MOVEd into WS-RETURN-MSG PIC X(75), losing the trailing five spaces. Note the nesting the source has and this case pins: at :764-766 the IF WS-RETURN-MSG-OFF guard wraps the FLAG, not the message, so FLG-ACCTFILTER-NOT-OK is set and FLG-CARDFILTER-NOT-OK is left BLANK.",
